  "requestTimestamp": "2026-07-19T05:43:57.604Z",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe estate tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law is a progressive rate ranging from 0% to 6% on the net estate value exceeding the threshold of ₱5,000,000.\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 84 of the NIRC, the estate tax is imposed on the transfer of the net estate of a decedent. The tax rates are structured progressively, with the first ₱5,000,000 of the net estate being exempt from tax, and the rates increasing for amounts above this threshold, culminating at a maximum rate of 6% for estates exceeding ₱10,000,000.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThis means that for estates valued at or below ₱5,000,000, no estate tax is due. For estates valued above this amount, the tax liability increases progressively, which can significantly impact estate planning and the distribution of assets to heirs. Executors and administrators must ensure compliance with these rates when filing estate tax returns.",
